# Captures from real projects never enter this repo — not committed, not kept locally. A capture is
# scoped to the repo it came from and is committed there, with that project. This directory is shared
# across every project and is public, so a capture in it would be global by construction. These lines
# are a backstop against an accidental commit; a capture found under them is deleted, not left here.
skills/*/references/local/
skills/*/local/
